Title: THE SIGNAL BOX
Credit: Written by
Author: Pure Alacrity example

[[HOW TO READ THIS
A branching example, not a real production. The viewer chooses once, at the level crossing. Each route has its own ending.]]

EXT. LEVEL CROSSING - NIGHT [N00]

A single red lamp swings over the rails. KIT (17) stands at the barrier with a bike. The signal box above her is dark.

KIT
Somebody's up there.

# PATHWAY · THE CROSSING

* CLIMB THE SIGNAL BOX — and find out who → [B01]
* RIDE ON — it is not your business → [END_ROAD]

EXT. SIGNAL BOX - STAIRS - NIGHT [B01]

Kit climbs. Every step rings. At the top, the door is open.

[[Handheld, one take up the stairs.]]

INT. SIGNAL BOX - NIGHT [END_LEVER]

An old lever frame. One lever is pulled half way. Kit finishes the pull.

> THE END <

EXT. COUNTRY ROAD - NIGHT [END_ROAD]

Kit rides away. Behind her, the red lamp goes out.

> THE END <
